# Local preparation note

The first preparation wrote two JSON files with Python's Windows newline
translation. Git stored LF, but the first local generation read CRLF. Its exact
input bytes are retained in initial-input-bytes and its actual registry digest
is recorded in generation-initial. Do not describe that invocation as using the
exact Git blob bytes merely because Git considered the working tree clean.

The first normalization copied the two Git blobs into the working tree, then
stopped at its clean-status assertion: Git still reported cached file-stat
changes, although the content diff was empty. The follow-on attempt to launch
generate-lf.py failed because the stopped setup had not created that file. No
production generation ran in that attempt. This paragraph summarizes tool
diagnostics; it is not a reconstructed raw stderr log.

Explicitly adding just those two files refreshed the index; the staged diff
remained empty. The corrected setup retained the previously saved CRLF bytes,
verified the actual LF blobs and clean status, then created a distinct LF run.
Both LF generation commands reproduced NodeLimit with no output stage. That
separate run is the fresh-checkout baseline for subsequent node-cap selection.
